FUNCTION_BLOCK "FB_RobotMove"
{ S7_Optimized_Access := 'TRUE' }
VERSION : 0.9
// the single movement. one request in, one move of program 20 on the robot, one state back.
// one file, one line of versions. 2026-11-04: the side folder "robot pose solution" was merged
// into this folder; the path mode is part of this block, switched by the request (intPathLen).
// v0.2 (2026-10-29): step 20 also waits until the robot shows program 20 initialized or
// finished (error 14 if not); step 40 keeps waiting while the robot repositions; t_run 3 s.
// v0.3 (2026-10-29): step 5 checks the start conditions of manual 9.4: setpoints active
// (error 5), override > 0 (error 8), program not paused (error 6).
// v0.4 (2026-11-03): the gate of the block goes on the bus in step 10 with the pose, settle
// 100 ms, step 30 only sets the start. the robot answered 125.57 "start edge ignored, not yet
// ready for movement" when gate and start left the plc in the same cycle.
// v0.5 (2026-11-03): the program stop before the start. after a jog, or after the setpoints were
// off, the robot reports "repositioning required" (PI 2.6), and a start would first drive it back
// to the point where it left the old path (manual 6.3, 6.6, 9.10). a program stop cancels that
// and puts the program back to "initialized" (9.8). step 10 goes to the new step 15 when the
// bit is set: State.xPrgStop TRUE on the bus (OB30 NW2 stop pin = Cmd.Stop OR State.xPrgStop),
// wait for initialized without the request, stop FALSE, then step 20. error 15 when the robot
// keeps the request for T_STOP. "program finished" is the normal state between two moves, a
// start works from it, nothing clears it.
// v0.6 (2026-11-02, path mode): a request may carry a path of up to 7 poses (udt_movereq v0.3,
// aoudtPath, intPathLen). step 5 checks every path pose, step 10 writes them to
// "DB_RobotPath".aoudtP[1..7] = srl pose[1..7], the module 1 standard path segments, before the
// gate opens. the block of program 20 then drives them in one program run: block 5 rectangle
// (7 lin), block 6 circle ccw (4 circ), block 7 circle cw. the engine does not know that either,
// it only waits longer: t_move_path instead of t_move. intPathLen = 0 is a single move exactly
// as before. new error 16: path longer than 7. the jobs set the path when "DB_Recipe".xPathMode is on.
// v0.7 (2026-11-06): blocks 6 and 7 get t_move_path even without a path. the drum job v0.6 sends
// the circle as ONE line of the robot (circ_var centerangle: the center in pose[51], the angle 360
// in real[52], no pose[1..7], intPathLen 0), and a full circle at a low override does not fit into
// t_move. one line in step 5, nothing else. (the file of the same version number in the critique
// folder is a different change of the user's, not this one)
// v0.8 (2026-11-09, the whole table): the time limit of a move grows with its length. one pin at
// the end, i_rMinSpeed = "DB_RobotMove".Cfg.rMinSpeed in mm/s. when it is > 0, step 5 adds the way
// of the move divided by it to t_move (or to t_move_path): the straight way from the actual pose to
// the target, the sum of the segments of a path, or the arc of a circle block (radius times the
// angle, 90 deg when none is given) when that is longer. 0 = exactly v0.7. a line of 4380 mm at
// 20 mm/s needs 219 s, more than t_move; with rMinSpeed 10 the limit for it is 60 + 438 s.
// v0.9 (2026-11-11, the review docs/engine_review_2026-11-04.md ported onto v0.8, no pin change):
//    step 0 owns the bus in idle: program number 20 and start FALSE every cycle, so no hand-set
//    start can stay on po 2.2 through a jog (the 11-05 second writer is gone, this closes the door).
//    the settle of step 20 counts from "program 20 ready", and ready also wants the control type
//    inactive (pi 4.8/9/10), the start condition of the state diagram (manual 6.3).
//    step 10 never sends a run number equal to what the robot still echoes in real[72]: after a
//    download the counter restarts while the robot keeps the old number, and step 40 would pass on
//    the stale "finished" before the robot has started.
//    step 5 keeps a copy of the request (udtReqAct); step 10 writes the copy, never the live input,
//    so the pose on the bus is always the pose that was checked (an auto switch or a typed pose in
//    the one cycle between the two steps could reach the bus unchecked).
//    block 5 without a path is refused, new error 17: it drives pose[1..7] as they stand in
//    db_robotpath, zeros after a download. blocks 6 and 7 run without a path since v0.7 and stay allowed.
//    step 5 also wants sto inactive and the output stage on (error 5).
//    step 50 notices a program stopped or paused by someone else, new error 18.
//    an error while the robot is in motion goes through the new step 95: program stop on the bus
//    until the robot stands, busy stays true meanwhile. before, "abort" only dropped start and
//    gates, and in automatic the robot finished the move while the engine said idle.
//
// goals.md section 5. this block knows only the contract of program 20 (section 5.1):
//    block n = gate bool[50+n]   target = pose[51]   parameters = real[51..53]
//    run number = real[54]       echo: real[71] = block that ran, real[72] = run number
//    path = pose[1..7]           (v0.6)
// it does not know what a block does. a new block in program 20 is a new number, not new code here.
//
// runs in ob1, one instance "IDB_RobotMove". ob30 keeps the bus and the status map.
// the only writer of: db_app.cmd.start, db_app.cmd.programnumber, db_app.cmd.override,
//                     db_app.srl.pose, db_app.srl.par, db_app.srl.gate, db_app.srl.gateenable,
//                     db_robotpath.aoudtp, db_robotpath.aorblend (v0.6)
//
// assumed types in db_app. if yours differ, change the io_ pins, nothing else:
//    Srl.Pose   Array[1..5] of Real        Srl.Par   Array[1..4] of Real
//    Srl.Gate   Array[1..8] of Bool        Srl.GateEnable   Bool
//    Cmd.Start  Bool    Cmd.ProgramNumber  Int    Cmd.Override  Int

   VAR_INPUT
      i_xStart : Bool;                   // rising edge starts the move
      i_xEnable : Bool;                  // moving allowed. falls while busy = abort, error 20
      i_xReset : Bool;                   // clears the error
      i_xSensorStop : Bool;              // reserved for the laser. read only when i_udtReq.xStopOnSensor
      i_udtReq : "UDT_MoveReq";          // the move: block, pose, parameters, override, path
      i_intBlocksInPrg20 : Int;          // "DB_RobotMove".Cfg.intBlocksInPrg20
      i_udtStatus : "UDT_RobotStatus";   // "DB_Robot".Status
      i_intEchoBlock : Int;              // srl real[71], "DB_MOVIKIT_ROBOTICS_Module2".SrlRealRaw[1]
      i_intEchoRun : Int;                // srl real[72], "DB_MOVIKIT_ROBOTICS_Module2".SrlRealRaw[2]
      i_rMinSpeed : Real;                // v0.8: "DB_RobotMove".Cfg.rMinSpeed, mm/s. the time limit of a move grows by its way / this. 0 = off
   END_VAR

   VAR_OUTPUT
      o_udtState : "UDT_MoveState";      // => "DB_RobotMove".State
   END_VAR

   VAR_IN_OUT
      io_aorSrlPose : Array[1..5] of Real;   // "DB_App".Srl.Pose   -> pose[51] x y z rotz roty
      io_aorSrlPar : Array[1..4] of Real;    // "DB_App".Srl.Par    -> real[51..54]
      io_aoxSrlGate : Array[1..8] of Bool;   // "DB_App".Srl.Gate   -> bool[51..58]
      io_xGateEnable : Bool;                 // "DB_App".Srl.GateEnable
      io_xStart : Bool;                      // "DB_App".Cmd.Start
      io_intPrgNr : Int;                     // "DB_App".Cmd.ProgramNumber
      io_intOverride : Int;                  // "DB_App".Cmd.Override
      io_aoudtPath : Array[1..7] of "UDT_Pose";   // "DB_RobotPath".aoudtP  -> pose[1..7]   (v0.6)
      io_aorPathBlend : Array[1..7] of Real;      // "DB_RobotPath".aorBlend -> segment blending   (v0.6)
   END_VAR

   VAR
      intStep : Int;                     // 0 idle, 5 check, 10 write, 15 program stop, 20 settle, 30 go, 40 running, 50 finished, 60 end, 90 error, 95 stop after an error
      xStartOld : Bool;
      intBlockAct : Int;                 // block of the move in progress
      intRunNr : Int;                    // 1..30000, one per move, echoed by the robot
      tMoveAct : Time;                   // v0.6: t_move for a single move, t_move_path for a path
      udtReqAct : "UDT_MoveReq";         // v0.9: the request as it was checked in step 5. step 10 writes this one
      tonSettle : TON_TIME;
      tonPrg : TON_TIME;
      tonRun : TON_TIME;
      tonMove : TON_TIME;
      tonStill : TON_TIME;
      tonStop : TON_TIME;                // v0.5
      tonErrStop : TON_TIME;             // v0.9: bounds step 95
   END_VAR

   VAR_TEMP
      tmp_xStartEdge : Bool;
      tmp_xFinished : Bool;
      tmp_xPrgReady : Bool;
      tmp_xRobotActive : Bool;           // v0.9: the robot runs its program, repositions or moves
      tmp_intErr : Int;
      tmp_i : Int;
      tmp_k : Int;
      tmp_rDist : Real;                  // v0.8: the way of the move, mm
      tmp_rArc : Real;                   // v0.8: the arc of a circle block, mm
      tmp_rPX : Real;                    // v0.8: the point the way is measured from
      tmp_rPY : Real;
      tmp_rPZ : Real;
   END_VAR

   VAR CONSTANT
      PRG_NR : Int := 20;                // the one robot program
      DEG_TO_RAD : Real := 0.017453293;  // v0.8: pi / 180, the arc of a circle block
      CIRC_FIRST : Int := 3;             // contract: blocks 3 and 4 are circles and need a radius in aorPar[1]
      CIRC_LAST : Int := 4;
      BLOCK_DRUM_CCW : Int := 6;         // v0.6: the drum circle blocks need a radius too. v0.7: and get t_move_path
      BLOCK_DRUM_CW : Int := 7;
      BLOCK_RECT : Int := 5;             // v0.9: block 5 drives pose[1..7] and needs a path in the request
      PATH_MAX : Int := 7;               // v0.6: pose[1..7], the seven segments of module 1
      T_SETTLE : Time := T#100ms;        // pose and gate on the bus before the start edge, rule 4 (100 ms since 2026-11-03)
      T_PRG : Time := T#3s;              // the robot must show program 20 initialized or finished within this
      T_RUN : Time := T#3s;              // "program running" must come within this, repositioning time not counted
      T_MOVE : Time := T#60s;            // a single move must finish within this
      T_MOVE_PATH : Time := T#300s;      // v0.6: a path of up to 7 moves must finish within this
      T_STILL : Time := T#200ms;         // finished and standstill must hold this long
      T_STOP : Time := T#2s;             // v0.5: after the program stop the robot must show initialized, no repositioning request, within this. v0.9: also bounds step 95
      RUNNR_MAX : Int := 30000;
   END_VAR

BEGIN
   // ---- edge and pulses ------------------------------------------------------
   #tmp_xStartEdge := #i_xStart AND NOT #xStartOld;
   #xStartOld := #i_xStart;
   #o_udtState.xDone := FALSE;

   // ---- reset, only out of the error step --------------------------------------
   IF #i_xReset AND #intStep = 90 THEN
      #o_udtState.xError := FALSE;
      #o_udtState.intErrId := 0;
      #o_udtState.uiMsgIdAtError := 0;
      #o_udtState.xPrgStop := FALSE;
      #intStep := 0;
   END_IF;

   // ---- timers, called every cycle so they never hold a stale state ----------------
   #tmp_xFinished := #i_udtStatus.xPrgFinished AND NOT #i_udtStatus.xMoving AND #i_udtStatus.intRemainingSeg = 0;
   // the robot has taken program 20 and can take a start: manual 6.3, a program can be
   // started when it is initialized or finished and the control type is inactive (v0.9)
   #tmp_xPrgReady := #i_udtStatus.intPrgNr = #PRG_NR
                     AND (#i_udtStatus.xPrgInitialized OR #i_udtStatus.xPrgFinished)
                     AND NOT #i_udtStatus.xPrgMode AND NOT #i_udtStatus.xJogMode AND NOT #i_udtStatus.xRefMode;
   #tmp_xRobotActive := #i_udtStatus.xPrgRunning OR #i_udtStatus.xRepositionActive OR #i_udtStatus.xMoving;
   // v0.9: the settle counts from "program 20 ready". before, it counted from the entry of
   // step 20, and after a program change the edge could follow "initialized" by one cycle
   #tonSettle(IN := #intStep = 20 AND #tmp_xPrgReady, PT := #T_SETTLE);
   #tonPrg(IN := #intStep = 20, PT := #T_PRG);
   // a start after jogging first repositions the robot onto the path. "running" comes after
   // that, so the run timer does not count while repositioning is active
   #tonRun(IN := #intStep = 40 AND NOT #i_udtStatus.xRepositionActive, PT := #T_RUN);
   IF #tMoveAct = T#0s THEN
      #tMoveAct := #T_MOVE;              // first cycle after a download
   END_IF;
   #tonMove(IN := #intStep = 50, PT := #tMoveAct);
   #tonStill(IN := #intStep = 50 AND #tmp_xFinished, PT := #T_STILL);
   #tonStop(IN := #intStep = 15, PT := #T_STOP);   // v0.5
   #tonErrStop(IN := #intStep = 95, PT := #T_STOP);   // v0.9

   // ---- abort while a move is in progress ------------------------------------------
   IF #intStep >= 10 AND #intStep <= 50 THEN
      #tmp_intErr := 0;
      IF NOT #i_udtStatus.xCommOK THEN
         #tmp_intErr := 7;
      ELSIF #i_udtStatus.xFault THEN
         #tmp_intErr := 21;
      ELSIF NOT #i_udtStatus.xAccessGranted THEN
         #tmp_intErr := 22;
      ELSIF NOT #i_xEnable THEN
         #tmp_intErr := 20;
      END_IF;
      IF #tmp_intErr <> 0 THEN
         #o_udtState.intErrId := #tmp_intErr;
         IF #tmp_xRobotActive THEN
            #intStep := 95;              // v0.9: stop the robot first
         ELSE
            #intStep := 90;
         END_IF;
      END_IF;
   END_IF;

   CASE #intStep OF
      0: // idle. v0.9: the bus is defined here too. program 20 stands on po 4 long before the
         // first move, and nothing else can leave a start on the bus
         #o_udtState.xBusy := FALSE;
         #io_intPrgNr := #PRG_NR;
         #io_xStart := FALSE;
         IF #tmp_xStartEdge AND #i_xEnable AND NOT #o_udtState.xError THEN
            #intStep := 5;
         END_IF;

      5: // check, one cycle, nothing touches the bus
         #tmp_intErr := 0;
         IF #i_udtReq.intBlock < 1 OR #i_udtReq.intBlock > 8 OR #i_udtReq.intBlock > #i_intBlocksInPrg20 THEN
            #tmp_intErr := 1;
         ELSE
            #tmp_intErr := "FC_PoseCheck"(i_udtPose := #i_udtReq.udtPose);   // 0, 2 or 3
         END_IF;
         // v0.6: every pose of the path is checked before anything goes out, rule 9
         IF #tmp_intErr = 0 THEN
            IF #i_udtReq.intPathLen < 0 OR #i_udtReq.intPathLen > #PATH_MAX THEN
               #tmp_intErr := 16;
            ELSE
               FOR #tmp_k := 1 TO #i_udtReq.intPathLen DO
                  IF #tmp_intErr = 0 THEN
                     #tmp_intErr := "FC_PoseCheck"(i_udtPose := #i_udtReq.aoudtPath[#tmp_k]);
                  END_IF;
               END_FOR;
            END_IF;
         END_IF;
         // v0.9: block 5 needs a path. without one the robot would drive pose[1..7] as they stand in
         // db_robotpath, zeros after a download or the corners of the last cube. blocks 6 and 7
         // run as one circle line without a path since v0.7 and are not touched by this
         IF #tmp_intErr = 0 AND #i_udtReq.intBlock = #BLOCK_RECT AND #i_udtReq.intPathLen = 0 THEN
            #tmp_intErr := 17;
         END_IF;
         IF #tmp_intErr = 0 THEN
            IF ((#i_udtReq.intBlock >= #CIRC_FIRST AND #i_udtReq.intBlock <= #CIRC_LAST)
                OR #i_udtReq.intBlock = #BLOCK_DRUM_CCW OR #i_udtReq.intBlock = #BLOCK_DRUM_CW)
               AND #i_udtReq.aorPar[1] <= 0.0 THEN
               #tmp_intErr := 4;
            ELSIF NOT #i_udtStatus.xCommOK THEN
               #tmp_intErr := 7;
            ELSIF NOT #i_udtStatus.xReady OR NOT #i_udtStatus.xReferenced OR NOT #i_udtStatus.xAutomatic
                  OR NOT #i_udtStatus.xAccessGranted OR #i_udtStatus.xFault
                  OR NOT #i_udtStatus.xSetpointActive
                  OR NOT #i_udtStatus.xStoInactive OR NOT #i_udtStatus.xPowerOn THEN   // v0.9: sto and output stage
               #tmp_intErr := 5;
            ELSIF #i_udtStatus.xMoving OR #i_udtStatus.xPrgRunning OR #i_udtStatus.xPrgPaused THEN
               #tmp_intErr := 6;
            ELSIF #i_udtReq.intOverride <= 0 AND #io_intOverride <= 0 THEN
               #tmp_intErr := 8;                // rule 7: override never 0, the robot would not move
            END_IF;
         END_IF;
         IF #tmp_intErr <> 0 THEN
            #o_udtState.intErrId := #tmp_intErr;
            #intStep := 90;
         ELSE
            #udtReqAct := #i_udtReq;            // v0.9: this is the request that was checked. nothing else goes out
            #o_udtState.xBusy := TRUE;
            #intBlockAct := #i_udtReq.intBlock;
            #o_udtState.intBlockActive := #intBlockAct;
            #o_udtState.intIdActive := #i_udtReq.intId;
            IF #i_udtReq.intPathLen > 0
               OR #i_udtReq.intBlock = #BLOCK_DRUM_CCW OR #i_udtReq.intBlock = #BLOCK_DRUM_CW THEN
               #tMoveAct := #T_MOVE_PATH;       // v0.6: up to seven moves in one program run. v0.7: the full circle of blocks 6 and 7 too
            ELSE
               #tMoveAct := #T_MOVE;
            END_IF;
            // v0.8: a long move gets more time, its way divided by the minimum speed of the configuration.
            // the way: from the actual pose to the target, or along the path segment by segment, or the
            // arc of a circle block when that is longer. 0 mm/s = the fixed limits of v0.7
            IF #i_rMinSpeed > 0.0 THEN
               #tmp_rPX := #i_udtStatus.udtPoseBcs.rX;
               #tmp_rPY := #i_udtStatus.udtPoseBcs.rY;
               #tmp_rPZ := #i_udtStatus.udtPoseBcs.rZ;
               IF #i_udtReq.intPathLen > 0 THEN
                  #tmp_rDist := 0.0;
                  FOR #tmp_k := 1 TO #i_udtReq.intPathLen DO
                     #tmp_rDist := #tmp_rDist + SQRT(SQR(#i_udtReq.aoudtPath[#tmp_k].rX - #tmp_rPX)
                                                   + SQR(#i_udtReq.aoudtPath[#tmp_k].rY - #tmp_rPY)
                                                   + SQR(#i_udtReq.aoudtPath[#tmp_k].rZ - #tmp_rPZ));
                     #tmp_rPX := #i_udtReq.aoudtPath[#tmp_k].rX;
                     #tmp_rPY := #i_udtReq.aoudtPath[#tmp_k].rY;
                     #tmp_rPZ := #i_udtReq.aoudtPath[#tmp_k].rZ;
                  END_FOR;
               ELSE
                  #tmp_rDist := SQRT(SQR(#i_udtReq.udtPose.rX - #tmp_rPX)
                                   + SQR(#i_udtReq.udtPose.rY - #tmp_rPY)
                                   + SQR(#i_udtReq.udtPose.rZ - #tmp_rPZ));
               END_IF;
               IF (#i_udtReq.intBlock >= #CIRC_FIRST AND #i_udtReq.intBlock <= #CIRC_LAST)
                  OR #i_udtReq.intBlock = #BLOCK_DRUM_CCW OR #i_udtReq.intBlock = #BLOCK_DRUM_CW THEN
                  IF ABS(#i_udtReq.aorPar[2]) > 0.0 THEN
                     #tmp_rArc := #i_udtReq.aorPar[1] * ABS(#i_udtReq.aorPar[2]) * #DEG_TO_RAD;
                  ELSE
                     #tmp_rArc := #i_udtReq.aorPar[1] * 90.0 * #DEG_TO_RAD;   // a quarter when the request names no angle
                  END_IF;
                  IF #tmp_rArc > #tmp_rDist THEN
                     #tmp_rDist := #tmp_rArc;
                  END_IF;
               END_IF;
               #tMoveAct := #tMoveAct + DINT_TO_TIME(REAL_TO_DINT(#tmp_rDist / #i_rMinSpeed * 1000.0));
            END_IF;
            #intStep := 10;
         END_IF;

      10: // write everything. gates closed, start off. v0.9: from the copy of step 5
         #intRunNr := #intRunNr + 1;
         IF #intRunNr > #RUNNR_MAX THEN
            #intRunNr := 1;
         END_IF;
         // v0.9: never the number the robot still echoes from before. after a download the
         // counter restarts while real[72] on the robot keeps the last number
         IF #intRunNr = #i_intEchoRun THEN
            #intRunNr := #intRunNr + 1;
            IF #intRunNr > #RUNNR_MAX THEN
               #intRunNr := 1;
            END_IF;
         END_IF;
         #o_udtState.intRunNr := #intRunNr;

         #io_intPrgNr := #PRG_NR;
         #io_aorSrlPose[1] := #udtReqAct.udtPose.rX;
         #io_aorSrlPose[2] := #udtReqAct.udtPose.rY;
         #io_aorSrlPose[3] := #udtReqAct.udtPose.rZ;
         #io_aorSrlPose[4] := #udtReqAct.udtPose.rRotZ;
         #io_aorSrlPose[5] := #udtReqAct.udtPose.rRotY;
         #io_aorSrlPar[1] := #udtReqAct.aorPar[1];
         #io_aorSrlPar[2] := #udtReqAct.aorPar[2];
         #io_aorSrlPar[3] := #udtReqAct.aorPar[3];
         #io_aorSrlPar[4] := INT_TO_REAL(#intRunNr);
         IF #udtReqAct.intOverride > 0 THEN
            #io_intOverride := LIMIT(MN := 1, IN := #udtReqAct.intOverride, MX := 100);   // rule 7: never 0
         END_IF;
         // v0.6: the path to pose[1..7]. unused segments hold the last pose, so every line of a
         // path block has a valid target even when the path is shorter than the block
         IF #udtReqAct.intPathLen > 0 THEN
            FOR #tmp_k := 1 TO #PATH_MAX DO
               IF #tmp_k <= #udtReqAct.intPathLen THEN
                  #io_aoudtPath[#tmp_k] := #udtReqAct.aoudtPath[#tmp_k];
               ELSE
                  #io_aoudtPath[#tmp_k] := #udtReqAct.aoudtPath[#udtReqAct.intPathLen];
               END_IF;
               #io_aorPathBlend[#tmp_k] := #udtReqAct.rBlend;
            END_FOR;
         END_IF;
         FOR #tmp_i := 1 TO 8 DO
            #io_aoxSrlGate[#tmp_i] := FALSE;
         END_FOR;
         #io_aoxSrlGate[#intBlockAct] := TRUE;   // the gate goes out with the pose, not with the start (2026-11-03)
         #io_xGateEnable := TRUE;
         #io_xStart := FALSE;
         IF #i_udtStatus.xRepositionRequired THEN
            #o_udtState.xPrgStop := TRUE;    // v0.5: cancel the way back to the old path first
            #intStep := 15;
         ELSE
            #intStep := 20;
         END_IF;

      15: // v0.5: program stop on the bus until the robot shows the program initialized and the
          // repositioning request gone (manual 9.8, 9.10). then the stop goes off, and step 20
          // keeps the start edge at least one settle time after its falling edge (manual 9.4)
         IF #i_udtStatus.xPrgInitialized AND NOT #i_udtStatus.xRepositionRequired
            AND NOT #i_udtStatus.xRepositionActive THEN
            #o_udtState.xPrgStop := FALSE;
            #intStep := 20;
         ELSIF #tonStop.Q THEN
            #o_udtState.xPrgStop := FALSE;
            #o_udtState.intErrId := 15;
            #intStep := 90;
         END_IF;

      20: // the pose and the gate sit on the bus for one settle time, rule 4, counted from the
          // moment the robot shows program 20 ready (v0.9). a program change takes the robot a moment
         IF #tonSettle.Q THEN
            #intStep := 30;
         ELSIF #tonPrg.Q THEN
            #o_udtState.intErrId := 14;
            #intStep := 90;
         END_IF;

      30: // the start edge. the gate is open since step 10
         #io_xStart := TRUE;
         #intStep := 40;

      40: // "program running" must be seen, rule 5.
          // a very short move can be over between two cycles: then finished + this run's
          // number already echoed in real[72] is the proof that the program ran
         IF #i_udtStatus.xPrgRunning THEN
            #intStep := 50;
         ELSIF #i_udtStatus.xPrgFinished AND #i_intEchoRun = #intRunNr THEN
            #intStep := 50;
         ELSIF #tonRun.Q THEN
            #o_udtState.intErrId := 11;
            IF #tmp_xRobotActive THEN
               #intStep := 95;
            ELSE
               #intStep := 90;
            END_IF;
         END_IF;

      50: // wait for finished and standstill, stable for t_still
          // later: the sensor stop branch goes here (i_udtReq.xStopOnSensor and i_xSensorStop)
         IF #tonStill.Q THEN
            #intStep := 60;
         ELSIF #i_udtStatus.xPrgInitialized OR #i_udtStatus.xPrgPaused THEN
            // v0.9: somebody else stopped or paused the program (old screen, robotmonitor).
            // the robot stands, the move is lost, say so now instead of after t_move
            #o_udtState.intErrId := 18;
            #intStep := 90;
         ELSIF #tonMove.Q THEN
            #o_udtState.intErrId := 12;
            IF #tmp_xRobotActive THEN
               #intStep := 95;
            ELSE
               #intStep := 90;
            END_IF;
         END_IF;

      60: // end. close everything, check the echo, report done
         #io_xStart := FALSE;
         #o_udtState.xPrgStop := FALSE;
         FOR #tmp_i := 1 TO 8 DO
            #io_aoxSrlGate[#tmp_i] := FALSE;
         END_FOR;
         #o_udtState.udtPoseAtEnd := #i_udtStatus.udtPoseBcs;
         IF #i_intEchoBlock <> #intBlockAct THEN
            #o_udtState.intErrId := 10;
            #intStep := 90;
         ELSIF #i_intEchoRun <> #intRunNr THEN
            #o_udtState.intErrId := 13;
            #intStep := 90;
         ELSE
            #o_udtState.xDone := TRUE;
            #o_udtState.xBusy := FALSE;
            #intStep := 0;
         END_IF;

      90: // error. close everything, stay here until reset
         #io_xStart := FALSE;
         #o_udtState.xPrgStop := FALSE;
         FOR #tmp_i := 1 TO 8 DO
            #io_aoxSrlGate[#tmp_i] := FALSE;
         END_FOR;
         #o_udtState.xBusy := FALSE;
         IF NOT #o_udtState.xError THEN
            #o_udtState.xError := TRUE;
            #o_udtState.uiMsgIdAtError := #i_udtStatus.uiMsgId;
            #o_udtState.udtPoseAtEnd := #i_udtStatus.udtPoseBcs;
         END_IF;

      95: // v0.9: an error came while the robot was in motion or in its program. in automatic the
          // start is an edge, dropping it stops nothing (manual 6.1.1, 9.8). program stop on the bus
          // until the robot stands, busy stays true so nobody teaches or starts into a moving robot.
          // the error is reported at once, the message id of this moment is kept
         #io_xStart := FALSE;
         FOR #tmp_i := 1 TO 8 DO
            #io_aoxSrlGate[#tmp_i] := FALSE;
         END_FOR;
         #o_udtState.xPrgStop := TRUE;
         IF NOT #o_udtState.xError THEN
            #o_udtState.xError := TRUE;
            #o_udtState.uiMsgIdAtError := #i_udtStatus.uiMsgId;
            #o_udtState.udtPoseAtEnd := #i_udtStatus.udtPoseBcs;   // the setpoint of this moment, not where the robot comes to rest
         END_IF;
         IF NOT #tmp_xRobotActive OR #tonErrStop.Q THEN
            #o_udtState.xPrgStop := FALSE;
            #intStep := 90;
         END_IF;
   END_CASE;

   #o_udtState.intStep := #intStep;

   // error numbers, goals.md 5.5
   //  1 block not 1..8 or not yet in program 20     10 wrong block echoed in real[71]
   //  2 x y z outside the limits (target or path)   11 no "program running" within t_run
   //  3 rotz roty outside the limits (target or path) 12 no "program finished" within t_move / t_move_path (+ way / rMinSpeed, v0.8)
   //  4 circle without radius (blocks 3, 4, 6, 7)   13 run number echo in real[72] is not this run
   //                                                 14 robot does not show program 20 ready (initialized or finished, control type inactive, v0.9)
   //                                                 15 program stop not taken, repositioning request stays (v0.5)
   //  5 not ready / referenced / automatic / access / setpoints / sto / output stage (v0.9)   16 path longer than 7 poses (v0.6)
   //  6 moving, program running or paused at start                17 block 5 without a path (v0.9)
   //  7 communication not ok                                      18 program stopped or paused by someone else during the move (v0.9)
   //  8 override is 0, nothing would move                         20 aborted, enable fell
   //                                                              21 aborted, robot fault
   //                                                              22 aborted, access lost (robotmonitor took over)
END_FUNCTION_BLOCK
